@* An extension brings its commands and shortcut (Ctrl+Shift+N), its sanitising policy, a click on a note that marks it
   as read, a context menu, a proofreader and text suggestions (Tab accepts). The case, the special characters, the
   table import and the display of the blocks are built-in commands. *@
<OmniStack Gap="OmniSpacing.Large">
    <OmniHtmlEditor Id="editor-extended"
                    @bind-Value="Extended"
                    Label="Annotated opinion"
                    Rows="6"
                    Commands="ExtendedCommands"
                    Extensions="[NoteExtension]" />

    @* The same proofreader on a text that starts locked: in read-only, nothing is underlined and the script keeps no
       answer; once unlocked, the misspellings are underlined. *@
    <OmniToggleButton Id="editor-locked-toggle" @bind-Value="LockedReadOnly">Read-only</OmniToggleButton>
    <OmniHtmlEditor Id="editor-locked"
                    @bind-Value="Locked"
                    Label="Proofread text, locked at first"
                    Rows="3"
                    ReadOnly="LockedReadOnly"
                    Commands="PaletteCommands"
                    Extensions="[ProofreadingExtension]" />
</OmniStack>
